   "text": {
    "L1": "Plants make their own food in their leaves using sunlight, water and air.",
    "L2": "Animals cannot make food, so they eat plants or other animals.",
    "L3": "A food chain shows who is eaten by whom.",
    "L4": "The arrow points from the food to the one who eats it.",
    "L5": "So grass is eaten by the grasshopper, and the grasshopper is eaten by the frog.",
    "L6": "The frog is eaten by the snake, so every living thing in this chain matters.",
    "L7": "If frogs disappear, grasshoppers increase and snakes have less food.",
    "L8": "Now put the chain in the correct order."
   },
